@startuml sequence-decision-email
' Spec 004 — an Admin decision and the email to the listing's owner (REQ-004-5..9).
' Amended by spec 005 (REQ-005-6, REQ-005-10): approval gives the listing its public address,
' and the approval email links to it.
' Parties: Admin's browser, JairojobsWeb (Admin listing LiveView), Jairojobs.Listings, Postgres,
' Mailer (Resend in production), the owner's inbox.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Admin
participant "Browser" as B
participant "JairojobsWeb\n(Admin.ListingLive)" as W
participant "Jairojobs.Listings" as L
database "Postgres" as DB
participant "ListingNotifier\n+ Jairojobs.Mailer" as M
participant "Resend" as R
participant "Owner's inbox" as IN

Admin -> B : Approve\n(or Reject / Take down with a reason,\nor Save changes)
B -> W : event
W -> L : approve_listing(scope, listing, owner_url, public_url)\n(reject_… / take_down_… / update_listing_as_admin,\neach with owner_url only)

group one transaction
  L -> DB : re-read the acting account,\nlock the listing row (FOR UPDATE)
  alt not an Admin
    L --> W : {:error, :unauthorized}
  else status is not the one the action needs
    L --> W : {:error, :not_pending}\n(:not_published / :not_editable)
    W --> B : "This listing is no longer waiting for approval."
  else region hidden (approve only)
    L --> W : {:error, :region_hidden}
  else reason or fields invalid
    L --> W : {:error, changeset}
    W --> B : validation error
  else allowed
    opt approve, or an edit that moves a Published listing (spec 005, REQ-005-6)
      L -> DB : lock the region's row; give the listing\nits public address there
    end
    L -> DB : update status, decided_at, decided_by_id\n(+ published_at and slug / reason / edited fields)
    DB --> L : committed
  end
end

note over L, DB : The decision is saved and committed\nbefore any email is attempted.

alt the Admin owns the listing, or an edit changed nothing
  L --> W : {:ok, listing, :own_listing}\n({:ok, listing, :unchanged})
  W --> B : confirmation
else someone else's listing
  L -> M : deliver_approved(owner, listing, public_url, owner_url)\n(rejected / taken down / edited: owner_url only)
  M -> R : send
  alt accepted
    R -> IN : "Your listing is published: <title>"
    M --> L : {:ok, email}
    L --> W : {:ok, listing, :sent}
    W --> B : confirmation
  else refused, unreachable, or raises
    M --> L : {:error, reason}
    L -> L : log the kind of email\nand the listing id, nothing else
    L --> W : {:ok, listing, :failed}
    W --> B : confirmation +\n"The employer could not be emailed."
  end
end

note over B, IN
  No second attempt. The owner still sees the outcome in My listings.
  The approval email carries two links: the listing's public page first,
  then the listing in My listings (spec 005, REQ-005-10). The others carry the second only.
  After approve and reject the Admin is back on the queue; after take down and edit, on the listing.
end note
@enduml
